{{- /*
  LazyVim writes this file itself when you toggle extras via :LazyExtras, so it
  is machine state, not shared config. It is deployed on ALL THREE machines, so
  every profile gets its own body -- an `else` fallback here would mean editing
  one machine's extras silently changed another's.

  Refresh after :LazyExtras with ./sync-nvim-state.sh (never `chezmoi add`,
  which would replace this dispatcher with a flat file).

  Two things to know before hand-editing any of the bodies:
    - Entries are FULL module names ("lazyvim.plugins.extras.lang.json").
    - "version" and "install_version" must both be present. Without "version"
      LazyVim runs its v0 migration, which prepends "lazyvim.plugins.extras."
      to every entry and silently breaks all of them. Without
      "install_version" >= 8 it treats the install as legacy and hands you
      fzf-lua + neo-tree instead of the snacks picker/explorer.

  sonbox is on LazyVim v16 (snacks stack, mini-hipatterns at its v16 util/
  path). The other two are still on their Dec 2025 state and list the old
  editor/ path; leave those alone until each machine is migrated.
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .profile "sonbox" -}}
{{-   template "nvim-lazyvim-sonbox.json" . -}}
{{- else if eq .profile "omarchy" -}}
{{-   template "nvim-lazyvim-omarchy.json" . -}}
{{- else -}}
{{-   template "nvim-lazyvim-rss-mac.json" . -}}
{{- end -}}
